; pi4V3dTri.pi4 - stage 4 of the V3D bring-up. IS THERE A TRIANGLE?
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THIS PROGRAM CLAIMS, AND WHAT IT REFUSES TO CLAIM
; ======================================================================
;
;  pi4V3dClear.pi4 got 4096 pixels of one colour out of the binner and
;  the renderer. A CLEAR NEEDS NO SHADER. This program is the first
;  thing here that runs a VERTEX SHADER and a FRAGMENT SHADER through
;  the graphics pipeline and rasterises a primitive.
;
;  THE PASS CRITERION IS COUNTED PIXELS AND A SHAPE, NOT A PICTURE.
;  A screenshot is not evidence and neither is "some pixels changed".
;  This program clears a 64 x 64 buffer to one colour, draws ONE
;  TRIANGLE in a second colour, reads back all 4096 words on the CPU
;  and reports:
;
;    * how many hold the triangle colour, the clear colour, the
;      poison it was filled with beforehand, and anything else;
;    * the BOUNDING BOX of the triangle-coloured pixels;
;    * how many pixels STRICTLY INSIDE the triangle are the wrong
;      colour, and how many STRICTLY OUTSIDE it are the wrong colour,
;      with a two-pixel margin either side of every edge so that no
;      fill-rule detail can decide the verdict;
;    * whether the unmapped guard page after the target was touched.
;
;  THE DIAGONAL EDGE IS THE POINT. A rectangle can be produced by a
;  blit, a clear with a scissor, or a store to the wrong address. A
;  triangle with a hypotenuse can only be produced by a rasteriser
;  fed by a shaded vertex, and the interior/exterior counts below
;  test exactly that: the pixels on the far side of the diagonal must
;  still be the clear colour.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE TWO COLOURS, AND WHY THE FRAGMENT VALUES ARE NOT n/255
; ======================================================================
;
;  clear    $44332211   R $11 G $22 B $33 A $44 - pi4V3dClear.pi4's
;  triangle $C0884422   R $22 G $44 B $88 A $C0
;
;  Eight distinct bytes across the two, so the channel order is proven
;  twice over and in the same read, and neither is the poison.
;
;  THE FRAGMENT SHADER WRITES f16 AND THE TILE BUFFER IS 8-BIT UNORM,
;  so each component makes a round trip f32 -> f16 -> unorm8 and the
;  rounding mode of the last step is not written down anywhere on this
;  disk. So the values are (n + 0.25) / 255 rather than n / 255:
;
;      $22 -> 34.25/255 = $3E09898A
;      $44 -> 68.25/255 = $3E890909
;      $88 -> 136.25/255 = $3F08C8C9
;      $C0 -> 192.25/255 = $3F410101
;
;  Through f16 those come back as 34.24, 68.23, 136.22 and 192.25 in
;  the 0..255 scale. Round-to-nearest gives 34, 68, 136 and 192, and
;  so does truncation. The test therefore cannot fail on a rounding
;  rule this project has not measured - which is a deliberate choice
;  to test the pipeline and not the converter, and it is stated here
;  so that nobody later reads the pass as evidence about rounding.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE SHADERS, AND WHY THEY DO NO ARITHMETIC
; ======================================================================
;
;  THE VERTICES ARE PRE-TRANSFORMED ON THE A72. That is the route
;  v3d-feasibility.md:264-267 proposes and it is the right one for a
;  first triangle: a shader that multiplies is a shader whose failure
;  has two explanations. These three shaders COPY.
;
;  THE SHADED VERTEX LAYOUT IS NOT NEGOTIABLE AND IT IS CITED.
;  Mesa mesa-24.3.4, src/broadcom/compiler/v3d_nir_lower_io.c:399-433:
;
;    coordinate shader   VPM 0-3 = Xc Yc Zc Wc, 4-5 = Xs Ys.  Six.
;    vertex shader       VPM 0-1 = Xs Ys, 2 = Zs, 3 = 1/Wc.   Four.
;
;  and :492-560 gives the arithmetic the shaders would have done:
;    Xs = f2i32(ffloor(Xc * viewport_x_scale * (1/Wc)))
;    Zs = Zc * z_scale * (1/Wc) + z_offset
;  with ffloor and not fround_even ON 4.2 SPECIFICALLY (:539-542).
;
;  Wc IS 1.0 FOR ALL THREE VERTICES, so 1/Wc is 1.0 and every one of
;  those multiplies is by one. The CPU does the rest.
;
;  Xs AND Ys ARE INTEGERS IN 1/256ths OF A PIXEL, RELATIVE TO THE
;  VIEWPORT CENTRE. The shader does not add the viewport offset - no
;  offset term appears in v3d_nir_lower_io.c's expression - so
;  VIEWPORT_OFFSET carries it, and its Fine X field is u14.8, i.e.
;  pixels times 256 (v3d_packet.xml:812). With a 64-wide surface the
;  centre is 32 pixels, so fine X and fine Y are 8192 and
;  CLIPPER_XY_SCALING's half-width, which is "in 1/256th of pixel"
;  (:822), is 8192.0f. The two have to agree and they are computed
;  from the same two numbers below.
;
;  THE THREE VERTICES, IN PIXELS: (8,8), (56,8), (8,56).
;  So Xs = (px - 32) * 256 and Ys = (py - 32) * 256, which is -6144,
;  +6144 and -6144 across X. A NEGATIVE INTEGER IS WHY THE ATTRIBUTE
;  RECORDS FOR SLOTS 4 AND 5 DECLARE `int` AND `read as int`: -6144 is
;  $FFFFE800 and +6144 is $00001800, and $00001800 read as a float is
;  a DENORMAL. If the vertex fetcher flushed denormals the triangle
;  would collapse to the viewport centre, which looks like a wrong
;  transform and is a wrong declaration. See V3dAttrRecordType().
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT IS UNPROVEN HERE EVEN IF EVERY PIXEL IS RIGHT
; ======================================================================
;
;   * THE Y DIRECTION IS NOT KNOWN IN ADVANCE and this program does
;     not pretend it is. The triangle is deliberately NOT symmetric,
;     the bounding box is printed, and the interior/exterior counts
;     are computed for BOTH conventions with the run saying which one
;     matched. Guessing and then "confirming" it would be worthless.
;   * ONE TILE. 64 x 64 is exactly one tile and one supertile, the
;     same reason pi4V3dClear.pi4 used it. Nothing here exercises the
;     supertile sweep or a partial tile.
;   * NO DEPTH, NO BLEND, NO TEXTURE, NO VARYINGS, NO CLIPPING WORK.
;     All three vertices are inside the clip volume, so the clipper's
;     output path is configured and never taken.
;   * THE SEVEN LDVPM OPERATIONS HAVE NO OFFLINE ORACLE. py-videocore6
;     cannot encode any of them; a64_v3d_qpu_check.py checks them
;     against its own reading of Mesa's tables and says so. THIS
;     PROGRAM IS THEIR ONLY REAL WITNESS - if the triangle appears in
;     the right place, LDVPMV_IN and STVPMV decoded the way both
;     readings thought.
;
; ======================================================================
;  RUNNING IT
; ======================================================================
;
;  PureMetalForge.exe --compile RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/pi4V3dTri.pi4 \
;      -t pi4 --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000 --entry-returns \
;      -o v3dtri.img
;  then send v3dtri.img to the resident monitor with a 35 second capture.
;
;  It prints a lot. Drive anvil with a fixed capture, not the default
;  four seconds - pi4V3dCsd.pi4's bench note applies here too.
; ======================================================================

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/mailbox.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3d.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4"

#UART_DR = $FE201000
#UART_FR = $FE201018

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE MEMORY MAP. Identity-mapped through the V3D MMU, VA = PA, the
;  same as every V3D probe before it. The guard page at $65C000 is
;  DELIBERATELY NOT MAPPED and sits immediately after the target.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#TRI_PT        = $640000
#TRI_PT_BYTES  = 16384
#TRI_ILLEGAL   = $648000
#TRI_BCL       = $650000
#TRI_TILELIST  = $651000
#TRI_RCL       = $652000
#TRI_TSTATE    = $653000
; The shader state record plus its eight attribute records. Page
; aligned, so 32-byte aligned, which GL_SHADER_STATE requires.
#TRI_SHREC     = $654000
; The vertex data, and the default attribute values 256 bytes into the
; same page.
#TRI_VERTS     = $655000
#TRI_DEFAULTS  = $655100
; The three uniform streams, 64 bytes apart.
#TRI_UNIF_CS   = $656000
#TRI_UNIF_VS   = $656040
#TRI_UNIF_FS   = $656080
; The three QPU programs, 512 bytes apart. Eight-byte aligned by
; construction; V3dQpuProgramBegin() refuses otherwise.
#TRI_CODE_CS   = $657000
#TRI_CODE_VS   = $657200
#TRI_CODE_FS   = $657400
#TRI_CODE_SLOT = 512
#TRI_TARGET    = $658000
#TRI_GUARD     = $65C000
; THE ENCODER CORPUS. A second shader state record with two attribute
; records, built with a NON-ZERO VALUE IN EVERY FIELD, never submitted
; and DELIBERATELY NOT MAPPED into the V3D page table.
;
; IT EXISTS BECAUSE A MUTATION RUN DEMANDED IT. Three faults injected
; into v3d.pi4's record encoders survived a64_v3d_tri_check.py's first
; pass and all three had the same shape: the field they corrupted is
; ZERO in this draw. The fragment shader has no varyings, so the
; varying count's shift does not matter; the three code addresses are
; page-plus-512 aligned, so the low-bit mask does not matter. That is
; stage 3's lesson arriving in a third file. A FIELD IS ONLY PINNED
; DOWN BY A VALUE WHOSE BITS ARE NOT ALL ZERO.
#TRI_CORPUS    = $65D000
#TRI_CORPUS_BYTES = 4096
#TRI_TALLOC    = $660000
#TRI_OVERFLOW  = $700000

#TRI_PAGE          = 4096
#TRI_BCL_BYTES     = 4096
#TRI_TL_BYTES      = 4096
#TRI_RCL_BYTES     = 4096
#TRI_TSTATE_BYTES  = 4096
#TRI_SHREC_BYTES   = 4096
#TRI_VERTS_BYTES   = 4096
#TRI_UNIF_BYTES    = 4096
#TRI_CODE_BYTES    = 4096
#TRI_TARGET_BYTES  = 16384
#TRI_GUARD_BYTES   = 4096
#TRI_TALLOC_BYTES  = $84000
#TRI_OVERFLOW_BYTES = 262144

#TRI_W      = 64
#TRI_H      = 64
#TRI_STRIDE = 256
#TRI_PIXELS = 4096

#TRI_CLEAR  = $44332211
#TRI_COLOR  = $C0884422
#TRI_POISON = $A5A5A5A5

; 1.0f, written into ZS_CLEAR_VALUES and never read - there is no
; depth buffer. Same value pi4V3dClear.pi4 uses and for the same
; reason.
#TRI_ZCLEAR = $3F800000

#TRI_F_ZERO   = $00000000
#TRI_F_ONE    = $3F800000
#TRI_F_P75    = $3F400000
#TRI_F_M75    = $BF400000
#TRI_F_8192   = $46000000

; The four fragment colour components. See the header.
#TRI_F_R = $3E09898A
#TRI_F_G = $3E890909
#TRI_F_B = $3F08C8C9
#TRI_F_A = $3F410101

; The TLB configuration word the fragment shader's TLBU write pulls
; out of the uniform stream. nir_to_vir.c:1856-1891 builds it:
;
;   0xffffff00                     the specifier register's fill
;   | TLB_SAMPLE_MODE_PER_PIXEL    1 << 2   = $04
;   | (7 - rt) << 3                7 << 3   = $38   (REVERSED: 7 = RT0)
;   | TLB_TYPE_F16_COLOR           3 << 6   = $C0
;   | TLB_F16_SWAP_HI_LO           1 << 1   = $02
;   | TLB_VEC_SIZE_4_F16           1 << 0   = $01
;
; which is $FFFFFFFF, and that is not a coincidence: the comment at
; nir_to_vir.c:1817-1820 says the register is "preloaded with
; 0xffffffff (0xff gets you normal vec4 f16 RT0 writes)". It is
; written explicitly anyway, exactly as Mesa writes it, because
; relying on a preloaded default is relying on nothing else having
; consumed a specifier first.
#TRI_TLB_CONF = $FFFFFFFF

; The three vertices, in PIXELS, and the viewport centre they are
; measured from. Everything below is derived from these five numbers.
#TRI_V0X = 8
#TRI_V0Y = 8
#TRI_V1X = 56
#TRI_V1Y = 8
#TRI_V2X = 8
#TRI_V2Y = 56
#TRI_CX  = 32
#TRI_CY  = 32

; The margin, in pixels, around every edge of the triangle inside
; which this program declines to have an opinion. TWO PIXELS, which
; is more than any fill rule can move an edge, so the interior and
; exterior counts below cannot be decided by one.
#TRI_MARGIN = 2

; 100 ms each. The kernel's own order of magnitude for a V3D wait.
#TRI_WAIT_US = 100000

; ======================================================================
;  PRINTING
; ======================================================================

Procedure PutC(c.i)
  Define f.i
  Repeat
    f = PeekN(#UART_FR)
  Until (f & 32) = 0
  PokeL(#UART_DR, c)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutS(*s)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    c = PeekA(*s + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
EndProcedure

Procedure PutNl()
  PutC(13) : PutC(10)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutHex(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      PutC(48 + n)
    Else
      PutC(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure PutDec(v.i)
  Define d.i
  Define started.i
  Define digit.i
  If v < 0
    PutC(45)
    v = 0 - v
  EndIf
  If v = 0
    PutC(48)
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  d = 1000000000000000000
  started = 0
  While d > 0
    digit = (v / d) % 10
    If digit <> 0 Or started = 1
      PutC(48 + digit)
      started = 1
    EndIf
    d = d / 10
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure PutPad(*name, width.i)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    c = PeekA(*name + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
  While i < width
    PutC(32)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure RowHex(*name, v.i)
  PutS("  ")
  PutPad(*name, 28)
  PutS("$")
  PutHex(v, 8)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure RowDec(*name, v.i)
  PutS("  ")
  PutPad(*name, 28)
  PutDec(v)
  PutNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure PutErr(e.i)
  Select e
    Case #V3D_OK
      PutS("OK")
    Case #V3D_ERR_NOINIT
      PutS("NOINIT - V3dInit() has not passed")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_OFF
      PutS("MMU_OFF - no V3D page table")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_FAULT
      PutS("MMU_FAULT - a page walk failed. See VIO_ADDR.")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_ALIGN
      PutS("MMU_ALIGN - an address is not aligned enough")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_RANGE
      PutS("MMU_RANGE - outside the page table, or page 0")
    Case #V3D_ERR_MMU_FLUSH
      PutS("MMU_FLUSH - the TLB clear never finished")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CACHE_TIMEOUT
      PutS("CACHE_TIMEOUT - the L2T clean never finished")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_ARGS
      PutS("CL_ARGS - a field or a buffer will not do")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_FULL
      PutS("CL_FULL - the list ran out of room")
    Case #V3D_ERR_CL_NOBUF
      PutS("CL_NOBUF - a packet with no list open")
    Case #V3D_ERR_BIN_TIMEOUT
      PutS("BIN_TIMEOUT - CLE_BFC never moved")
    Case #V3D_ERR_BIN_OOM
      PutS("BIN_OOM - the tile allocation pool ran out")
    Case #V3D_ERR_RENDER_TIMEOUT
      PutS("RENDER_TIMEOUT - CLE_RFC never moved")
    Case #V3D_ERR_JOB_BUSY
      PutS("JOB_BUSY - the render was offered before the bin finished")
    Default
      PutS("code ")
      PutDec(e)
  EndSelect
EndProcedure

Procedure PutQpuErr(e.i)
  Select e
    Case #V3DQ_OK
      PutS("OK")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_ADD_OP
      PutS("ADD_OP - that ADD operation is not encoded")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_SIG
      PutS("SIG - no 4.2 code for that signal combination")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_RANGE
      PutS("RANGE - a waddr, mux or raddr is out of its field")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_FULL
      PutS("FULL - the program buffer has no room")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_NOBUF
      PutS("NOBUF - V3dQpuProgramBegin() was never called")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_HAZARD
      PutS("HAZARD - a p37 restriction, rule ")
      PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName())
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_VPM_DEST
      PutS("VPM_DEST - a magic destination on a VPM load")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_PACK
      PutS("PACK - an output pack this operation cannot take")
    Case #V3DQ_ERR_UNPACK
      PutS("UNPACK - an input unpack this operation cannot take")
    Default
      PutS("code ")
      PutDec(e)
  EndSelect
EndProcedure

; A control list or a record, as bytes, sixteen to a line. Printed in
; full every run: it is the only evidence that survives a hang, and it
; is what makes a claim about "what the lists contain" checkable by
; somebody who was not at the bench.
Procedure DumpBytes(base.i, len.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < len
    If (i % 16) = 0
      PutS("  ")
      PutHex(base + i, 8)
      PutS(":")
    EndIf
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekA(base + i), 2)
    i = i + 1
    If (i % 16) = 0
      PutNl()
    EndIf
  Wend
  If (len % 16) <> 0
    PutNl()
  EndIf
EndProcedure

; A QPU program, one 64-bit instruction per line, high half first the
; way every V3D disassembler prints it.
Procedure DumpProgram(base.i, count.i)
  Define i.i
  i = 0
  While i < count
    PutS("  Q ")
    PutDec(i)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekN(base + (i * 8) + 4), 8)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(PeekN(base + (i * 8)), 8)
    PutNl()
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE THREE SHADERS
;
;  Every one of them is uniform loads, VPM traffic and a thread end.
;  No arithmetic. See the header for why.
;
;  THE UNIFORM STREAM IS READ IN PROGRAM ORDER. Each LDUNIFRF consumes
;  the next word, and the fragment shader's write to TLBU consumes one
;  more without an LDUNIFRF at all - v3d_qpu_magic_waddr_loads_unif()
;  (qpu_instr.c:646-658) names VPMU, TLBU, TMUAU and SYNCU as the four
;  magic addresses that pull from the uniform FIFO. So the streams
;  built by BuildUniforms() are laid out in the order the shaders
;  touch them and nowhere else.
; ======================================================================

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE COORDINATE SHADER. Six values in, six values out.
;
;  Reads VPM input slots 0..5 - Xc Yc Zc Wc Xs Ys - and writes them to
;  VPM output slots 0..5, which is the coordinate shader's shaded
;  vertex layout unchanged (v3d_nir_lower_io.c:412-419).
;
;  IT IS A SINGLE-SEGMENT PROGRAM. It never switches threads, so it is
;  spawned already in the final thread section and its whole thread
;  end is one THRSW and three NOPs - nir_to_vir.c:4886-4890 and
;  qpu_validate.c:430. The shader state record's "coordinate shader
;  start in final thread section" bit says the same thing and the two
;  MUST agree; V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg() cannot check the record and the
;  record cannot check the program.
;
;  VPMWT AFTER THE LAST STORE AND BEFORE THE THREAD END is GFXH-1684:
;  "VPM writes need to be complete by the end of the shader",
;  nir_to_vir.c:2070-2077, and emit_vert_end() is called after the
;  last THRSW is placed and before the scheduler appends the program
;  end (nir_to_vir.c:4959-4979, qpu_schedule.c:3052-3055).
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildCoordShader()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TRI_CODE_CS, #TRI_CODE_SLOT, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; rf0..rf5 = the constants 0..5, from the uniform stream. Mesa does
  ; exactly this - vir_LDVPMV_IN(c, vir_uniform_ui(c, index)),
  ; nir_to_vir.c:2826-2828 - rather than using a small immediate,
  ; and following it removes a guess about whether LDVPMV's offset
  ; operand may come from the small-immediate slot.
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, k, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; rf8..rf13 = VPM input 0..5. Mux A reads RADDR_A, which holds the
  ; register with the offset in it.
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 8 + k, #V3DQ_MUX_A, k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; VPM output 0..5 = rf8..rf13. STVPMV takes the SLOT INDEX first and
  ; the VALUE second - vir_STVPMV(c, vpm_index, val),
  ; nir_to_vir.c:2058 - and it has no destination at all: the waddr
  ; field carries the operation.
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, k, 8 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_VPMWT, #V3DQ_WADDR_NOP, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE VERTEX SHADER. Four values out of eight in.
;
;  Reads VPM input slots 4..7 - Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc - and writes them to VPM
;  output slots 0..3, which is the NON-coord layout
;  (v3d_nir_lower_io.c:418-424). The vertex shader's VPM INPUT holds
;  all eight values because its attribute records say so; the
;  coordinate shader's holds six. They are separate blocks.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildVertexShader()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TRI_CODE_VS, #TRI_CODE_SLOT, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  k = 0
  While k < 8
    r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, k, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; rf8..rf11 = VPM input 4..7.
  k = 0
  While k < 4
    r = V3dQpuLdvpm(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 8 + k, #V3DQ_MUX_A, 4 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; VPM output 0..3 = rf8..rf11.
  k = 0
  While k < 4
    r = V3dQpuStvpm(#V3DQ_A_STVPMV, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, k, 8 + k)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_VPMWT, #V3DQ_WADDR_NOP, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE FRAGMENT SHADER. Four uniforms in, one pixel out.
;
;  TWO VFPACKs, EXACTLY AS MESA EMITS THEM for an 8-bit render target
;  (nir_to_vir.c:1930-1942): the first writes TLBU and carries the
;  configuration word, the second writes TLB. Each VFPACK packs two
;  f32 lanes into one 2 x f16 result, so (r,g) then (b,a) is four
;  components in two instructions.
;
;  THE TLB WRITES COME AFTER THE LAST THREAD SWITCH AND THAT IS THE
;  ONE STRUCTURAL THING IN THIS SHADER. nir_to_vir.c:4959 is a comment
;  that says so in as many words - "Emit the last THRSW before STVPM
;  and TLB writes" - because the tile buffer is a shared resource and
;  the final thread section is where the scoreboard lock is held.
;  Unlike the other two shaders this one is therefore NOT single
;  segment, and the shader record's "fragment shader start in final
;  thread section" bit is clear to match.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildFragmentShader()
  Define r.i
  Define k.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#TRI_CODE_FS, #TRI_CODE_SLOT, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; rf0..rf3 = R, G, B, A.
  k = 0
  While k < 4
    r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, k, 0)
    If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
    k = k + 1
  Wend

  ; The last-THRSW pair and its two delay slots.
  r = V3dQpuLastThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  ; TLBU first: the write pulls the configuration word out of the
  ; uniform stream by itself.
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLBU, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 0, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  r = V3dQpuVfpack(#V3DQ_WADDR_TLB, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B, 2, 3)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  r = V3dQpuProgramEndThrsw()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE DATA
; ======================================================================

; One vertex, eight 32-bit values, in the order the attribute records
; declare them: Xc Yc Zc Wc Xs Ys Zs 1/Wc.
Procedure PutVertex(n.i, xc.i, yc.i, xs.i, ys.i)
  Define b.i
  b = #TRI_VERTS + (n * 32)
  PokeN(b +  0, xc)
  PokeN(b +  4, yc)
  PokeN(b +  8, #TRI_F_ZERO)   ; Zc, and therefore Zw = 0 with Wc = 1
  PokeN(b + 12, #TRI_F_ONE)    ; Wc
  PokeN(b + 16, xs)            ; Xs, an INTEGER in 1/256 pixel
  PokeN(b + 20, ys)            ; Ys
  PokeN(b + 24, #TRI_F_ZERO)   ; Zs = Zc * 1 + 0
  PokeN(b + 28, #TRI_F_ONE)    ; 1/Wc
EndProcedure

Procedure BuildVerts()
  Define i.i
  ; Xs = (px - 32) * 256, and the subtraction is what VIEWPORT_OFFSET
  ; puts back.
  PutVertex(0, #TRI_F_M75, #TRI_F_M75, (#TRI_V0X - #TRI_CX) * 256, (#TRI_V0Y - #TRI_CY) * 256)
  PutVertex(1, #TRI_F_P75, #TRI_F_M75, (#TRI_V1X - #TRI_CX) * 256, (#TRI_V1Y - #TRI_CY) * 256)
  PutVertex(2, #TRI_F_M75, #TRI_F_P75, (#TRI_V2X - #TRI_CX) * 256, (#TRI_V2Y - #TRI_CY) * 256)

  ; The default attribute values. Mesa always supplies an address
  ; (v3dx_draw.c:701-703) and the hardware reads from it for any
  ; component a shader asks for that the record does not supply.
  ; Nothing here asks for one; it is (0,0,0,1) because that is what a
  ; missing vec4 should be.
  PokeN(#TRI_DEFAULTS +  0, #TRI_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TRI_DEFAULTS +  4, #TRI_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TRI_DEFAULTS +  8, #TRI_F_ZERO)
  PokeN(#TRI_DEFAULTS + 12, #TRI_F_ONE)
EndProcedure

Procedure BuildUniforms()
  Define k.i
  ; The coordinate shader loads six constants, 0..5.
  k = 0
  While k < 6
    PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_CS + (k * 4), k)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  ; The vertex shader loads eight, 0..7.
  k = 0
  While k < 8
    PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_VS + (k * 4), k)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  ; The fragment shader loads four colour components and then the TLB
  ; configuration word, WHICH IS FIFTH BECAUSE THE TLBU WRITE IS THE
  ; FIFTH THING TO TOUCH THE STREAM.
  PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_FS +  0, #TRI_F_R)
  PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_FS +  4, #TRI_F_G)
  PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_FS +  8, #TRI_F_B)
  PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_FS + 12, #TRI_F_A)
  PokeN(#TRI_UNIF_FS + 16, #TRI_TLB_CONF)
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE SHADER STATE RECORD AND EIGHT ATTRIBUTE RECORDS.
;
;  ONE ATTRIBUTE RECORD PER VALUE, and that is a deliberate choice
;  rather than a natural one. A single record with a vec size of four
;  would be fewer records - and "vec size" is a two-bit field whose
;  encoding for four components is not stated in v3d_packet.xml and
;  is not written anywhere else on this disk. Mesa's own dummy record
;  (v3dx_draw.c:877-887) uses vec_size 1 with one value read, which
;  pins ONE point of that encoding and no other. So every attribute
;  here is one 32-bit value with vec size 1, which is the only shape
;  this project can cite.
;
;  THE COORDINATE SHADER READS SIX AND THE VERTEX SHADER READS EIGHT.
;  The VPM offset for value k is the SUM of the previous attributes'
;  counts (nir_to_vir.c:2810-2824), and with one value each that sum
;  is k - which is why the shaders can use the constants 0..7 as
;  their offsets directly. Records 6 and 7 have a coordinate-shader
;  count of ZERO, so the coordinate shader's VPM input block is six
;  values and its offsets 0..5 mean the same six values.
;
;  GFXH-930 is satisfied: records 0..5 are read by both phases.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE ENCODER CORPUS RECORD. See the memory map for why it exists.
;
;  EVERY VALUE HERE IS CHOSEN SO THAT A WRONG SHIFT MOVES IT. The
;  varying count is $AD rather than zero; the eight VPM nibbles are
;  eight DIFFERENT numbers so a transposed pair is visible; the
;  minus_one on the two input-segment counts is exercised at 9 and 16
;  rather than at 1, where minus one and no minus one look alike; and
;  THE THREE CODE ADDRESSES ARE EIGHT-BYTE ALIGNED AND NOT SIXTEEN,
;  which is the one case that tells a $FFFFFFF8 mask from a $FFFFFFF0
;  one. The three flag triples are all different so that the fourWay /
;  finalSeg / propagateNans bits cannot be transposed unnoticed.
;
;  IT IS BUILT FIRST, BEFORE THE REAL RECORD, because
;  V3dShaderRecordBegin() takes over the library's one record cursor
;  and the real record must be the one V3dShaderRecordAddr() names
;  when the bin list is written.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildCorpusRecord()
  Define r.i
  r = V3dShaderRecordBegin(#TRI_CORPUS, 2)
  If r <> #V3D_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf
  V3dShaderRecordFlags(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, $AD)
  V3dShaderRecordVpm(3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 16)
  V3dShaderRecordDefaults($12345678)
  V3dShaderRecordFragment($0ABCDEF8, $13579BDC, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordVertex($01234568, $2468ACE0, 0, 1, 0)
  V3dShaderRecordCoord($0FEDCBA8, $3141592C, 1, 1, 0)
  V3dAttrRecord(0, $ABCDEF00, $00010203, $04050607, 13, 7)
  V3dAttrRecordType(0, 2, #V3D_ATTR_SHORT, 1, 1, 0, $BEEF)
  V3dAttrRecord(1, $76543210, $0A0B0C0D, $0E0F1011, 5, 12)
  V3dAttrRecordType(1, 3, #V3D_ATTR_BYTE, 0, 1, 1, $1234)
  If V3dShaderRecordOk() = 0
    ProcedureReturn #V3D_ERR_CL_ARGS
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn #V3D_OK
EndProcedure

Procedure.i BuildRecords(csCount.i, vsCount.i)
  Define r.i
  Define k.i
  Define cs.i

  r = V3dShaderRecordBegin(#TRI_SHREC, 8)
  If r <> #V3D_OK : ProcedureReturn r : EndIf

  V3dShaderRecordFlags(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0)
  ; Shared VPM segments, one sector each way, As = 1 and Ve = 0.
  ; Mesa mesa-24.3.4 src/broadcom/compiler/vir.c:2508-2515 for As and Ve, :843-859 for
  ; the segment sizes and for separate_segments being forced false.
  V3dShaderRecordVpm(1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordDefaults(#TRI_DEFAULTS)
  V3dShaderRecordFragment(#TRI_CODE_FS, #TRI_UNIF_FS, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordVertex(#TRI_CODE_VS, #TRI_UNIF_VS, 1, 1, 1)
  V3dShaderRecordCoord(#TRI_CODE_CS, #TRI_UNIF_CS, 1, 1, 1)

  k = 0
  While k < 8
    cs = 1
    If k >= csCount
      cs = 0
    EndIf
    V3dAttrRecord(k, #TRI_VERTS + (k * 4), 32, $FFFFFF, cs, 1)
    k = k + 1
  Wend
  ; Slots 4 and 5 are Xs and Ys and they are SIGNED INTEGERS. See the
  ; header - $00001800 read as a float is a denormal.
  V3dAttrRecordType(4, 1, #V3D_ATTR_INT, 1, 0, 1, 0)
  V3dAttrRecordType(5, 1, #V3D_ATTR_INT, 1, 0, 1, 0)

  If V3dShaderRecordOk() = 0
    ProcedureReturn #V3D_ERR_CL_ARGS
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn #V3D_OK
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  VERIFICATION
; ======================================================================

Global nTri.i     = 0
Global nClear.i   = 0
Global nPoison.i  = 0
Global nOther.i   = 0
Global firstOther.i = -1
Global firstOtherVal.i = 0
Global minX.i = 9999
Global maxX.i = -1
Global minY.i = 9999
Global maxY.i = -1
Global guardTouched.i = 0

; The two conventions, counted separately. `dir` 0 means the shaded Ys
; increases with the row index the store writes; `dir` 1 means it
; decreases. NOTHING ON THIS DISK SAYS WHICH, so both are computed and
; the run says which one matched.
Global insideBad0.i  = 0
Global outsideBad0.i = 0
Global insideN0.i    = 0
Global outsideN0.i   = 0
Global insideBad1.i  = 0
Global outsideBad1.i = 0
Global insideN1.i    = 0
Global outsideN1.i   = 0

Procedure.i PixelAt(x.i, y.i)
  ProcedureReturn PeekN(#TRI_TARGET + (y * #TRI_STRIDE) + (x * 4))
EndProcedure

; Is (x,y) strictly inside the triangle (8,8)-(56,8)-(8,56) by at
; least `m` pixels on every edge? The three edges are x = 8, y = 8 and
; x + y = 64, so the test is three inequalities and no arithmetic that
; can overflow.
Procedure.i InsideBy(x.i, y.i, m.i)
  If x < (#TRI_V0X + m)
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If y < (#TRI_V0Y + m)
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If (x + y) > ((#TRI_V1X + #TRI_V1Y) - m)
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

; Is (x,y) strictly OUTSIDE the same triangle by at least `m` pixels?
; It is outside if it is on the wrong side of ANY edge by the margin.
Procedure.i OutsideBy(x.i, y.i, m.i)
  If x < (#TRI_V0X - m)
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  If y < (#TRI_V0Y - m)
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  If (x + y) > ((#TRI_V1X + #TRI_V1Y) + m)
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

Procedure Verify()
  Define x.i
  Define y.i
  Define v.i
  Define sy.i

  y = 0
  While y < #TRI_H
    x = 0
    While x < #TRI_W
      v = PixelAt(x, y)
      If v = #TRI_COLOR
        nTri = nTri + 1
        If x < minX : minX = x : EndIf
        If x > maxX : maxX = x : EndIf
        If y < minY : minY = y : EndIf
        If y > maxY : maxY = y : EndIf
      ElseIf v = #TRI_CLEAR
        nClear = nClear + 1
      ElseIf v = #TRI_POISON
        nPoison = nPoison + 1
      Else
        nOther = nOther + 1
        If firstOther < 0
          firstOther = (y * #TRI_W) + x
          firstOtherVal = v
        EndIf
      EndIf

      ; Convention 0: the store's row y IS the shaded Ys row.
      If InsideBy(x, y, #TRI_MARGIN) = 1
        insideN0 = insideN0 + 1
        If v <> #TRI_COLOR
          insideBad0 = insideBad0 + 1
        EndIf
      EndIf
      If OutsideBy(x, y, #TRI_MARGIN) = 1
        outsideN0 = outsideN0 + 1
        If v <> #TRI_CLEAR
          outsideBad0 = outsideBad0 + 1
        EndIf
      EndIf

      ; Convention 1: the store's row y is (height - 1 - Ys row).
      sy = (#TRI_H - 1) - y
      If InsideBy(x, sy, #TRI_MARGIN) = 1
        insideN1 = insideN1 + 1
        If v <> #TRI_COLOR
          insideBad1 = insideBad1 + 1
        EndIf
      EndIf
      If OutsideBy(x, sy, #TRI_MARGIN) = 1
        outsideN1 = outsideN1 + 1
        If v <> #TRI_CLEAR
          outsideBad1 = outsideBad1 + 1
        EndIf
      EndIf

      x = x + 1
    Wend
    y = y + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

Procedure VerifyGuard()
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  i = 0
  n = #TRI_GUARD_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    If PeekN(#TRI_GUARD + (i * 4)) <> #TRI_POISON
      guardTouched = guardTouched + 1
    EndIf
    i = i + 1
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  MAIN
; ======================================================================

Procedure Main()
  Define r.i
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  Define csBytes.i
  Define vsBytes.i
  Define fsBytes.i
  Define ok.i

  PutNl()
  PutS("=== Pi 4 V3D stage 4 - one triangle, 64x64, counted ===")
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  0. Stage 0. A precondition and not a formality: V3D 7.1 puts
  ;     different registers at these offsets and the CLE is a bus
  ;     master.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dInit()
  PutS("0   stage 0: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("HUB_IDENT1", V3dIdent1())
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: STAGE0")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  1. THE THREE QPU PROGRAMS, BUILT AND PRINTED FIRST.
  ;
  ;     Before any hardware state exists, because a program that
  ;     refuses to assemble is a finding that should not need a
  ;     working MMU to reach, and because a listing already on the
  ;     wire survives a hang later.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("1   the shaders")
  PutNl()

  r = BuildCoordShader()
  csBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    coordinate shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", csBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TRI_CODE_CS, csBytes / 8)

  r = BuildVertexShader()
  vsBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    vertex shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", vsBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TRI_CODE_VS, vsBytes / 8)

  r = BuildFragmentShader()
  fsBytes = V3dQpuProgramBytes()
  PutS("    fragment shader: ")
  PutQpuErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("verdict: SHADER")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("instructions", fsBytes / 8)
  DumpProgram(#TRI_CODE_FS, fsBytes / 8)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  2. The frame geometry, printed before anything is built from it.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRenderBegin(#TRI_W, #TRI_H, #V3D_OFMT_RGBA8)
  PutS("2   the frame: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: GEOMETRY")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("tile width", V3dTileW())
  RowDec("tile height", V3dTileH())
  RowDec("tiles across", V3dTilesX())
  RowDec("tiles down", V3dTilesY())
  RowDec("RT internal type", V3dRtInternalType())
  RowDec("RT internal bpp", V3dRtInternalBpp())
  RowDec("tile alloc needed", V3dTileAllocNeeded())
  RowDec("tile alloc given", #TRI_TALLOC_BYTES)
  PutNl()

  r = V3dRenderTarget(#TRI_TARGET, #TRI_TARGET_BYTES, #V3D_MEMFMT_RASTER, #TRI_STRIDE, 0)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the render target: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  V3dRenderClear(#TRI_CLEAR, #TRI_ZCLEAR, 0)
  r = V3dRenderPool(#TRI_TALLOC, #TRI_TALLOC_BYTES, #TRI_TSTATE, #TRI_TSTATE_BYTES)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the pools: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dBinOverflow(#TRI_OVERFLOW, #TRI_OVERFLOW_BYTES)
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    the overflow pool: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  3. THE DATA AND THE RECORDS.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BuildVerts()
  BuildUniforms()

  ; POISON BOTH RECORD PAGES BEFORE EITHER IS BUILT. Twenty fields of
  ; the record are booleans nothing here sets, and the hardware reads
  ; all of them; V3dShaderRecordBegin() zeroes the record for exactly
  ; that reason. Over zeroed DRAM a missing zeroing pass is invisible,
  ; which is what let a mutant that deleted it survive.
  i = 0
  n = #TRI_CORPUS_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TRI_CORPUS + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    PokeN(#TRI_SHREC + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  r = BuildCorpusRecord()
  PutS("3   the encoder corpus record: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: CORPUS")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("corpus bytes", V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  DumpBytes(#TRI_CORPUS, V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  PutNl()

  r = BuildRecords(6, 8)
  PutS("3b  the shader state record: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RECORD")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowHex("record", V3dShaderRecordAddr())
  RowDec("record + attrs, bytes", V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dShaderRecordAddr(), V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  PutS("    the three vertices, eight words each:")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TRI_VERTS, 96)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  4. POISON THE TARGET AND THE GUARD PAGE.
  ;
  ;     Poisoning rather than only checking for the two colours is
  ;     what makes "wrote nothing", "wrote zeros" and "wrote part of
  ;     it" three distinguishable answers.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  i = 0
  n = #TRI_TARGET_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TRI_TARGET + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  i = 0
  n = #TRI_GUARD_BYTES / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TRI_GUARD + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  i = 0
  n = 4096 / 4
  While i < n
    PokeN(#TRI_TALLOC + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    PokeN(#TRI_TSTATE + (i * 4), #TRI_POISON)
    i = i + 1
  Wend

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  5. THE V3D MMU. Every address the CLE, the PTB, the VCD, the QPU
  ;     and the TLB touch is VIRTUAL.
  ;
  ;     THE FIVE NEW MAPPINGS ARE THE STAGE-4 ONES: the shader state
  ;     record, the vertex data, the uniform streams and the QPU
  ;     programs. A clear needed none of them.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutS("5   the V3D MMU: ")
  r = V3dMmuInit(#TRI_PT, #TRI_PT_BYTES, #TRI_ILLEGAL)
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: MMU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_BCL, #TRI_BCL, #TRI_BCL_BYTES)
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_TILELIST, #TRI_TILELIST, #TRI_TL_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_RCL, #TRI_RCL, #TRI_RCL_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_TSTATE, #TRI_TSTATE, #TRI_TSTATE_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_SHREC, #TRI_SHREC, #TRI_SHREC_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_VERTS, #TRI_VERTS, #TRI_VERTS_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_UNIF_CS, #TRI_UNIF_CS, #TRI_UNIF_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_CODE_CS, #TRI_CODE_CS, #TRI_CODE_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_TARGET, #TRI_TARGET, #TRI_TARGET_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_TALLOC, #TRI_TALLOC, #TRI_TALLOC_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r = #V3D_OK
    r = V3dMmuMap(#TRI_OVERFLOW, #TRI_OVERFLOW, #TRI_OVERFLOW_BYTES)
  EndIf
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("    mapping: ") : PutErr(r) : PutNl()
    PutS("verdict: MMU")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("pages mapped", V3dMmuPagesMapped())
  RowHex("PTE for the guard page", V3dMmuEntry(#TRI_GUARD))
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  6. THE BIN LIST - the prologue, the draw state, and the primitive.
  ;
  ;     THE ORDER IS MESA'S, from v3dX(emit_state) (v3dx_emit.c:256 to
  ;     :684 in source order), then v3d_emit_gl_shader_state
  ;     (v3dx_draw.c:891-908), then the primitive (:1330-1334).
  ;     Nothing here chose it.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dBclBegin(#TRI_BCL, #TRI_BCL_BYTES)
  If r = #V3D_OK
    ; The clip window is the whole surface. v3dx_emit.c:243-263.
    V3dClClipWindow(0, 0, #TRI_W, #TRI_H)

    ; BOTH FACING BITS ARE SET, so a winding this program has not
    ; reasoned about cannot cull the triangle. Depth-test function
    ; ALWAYS, which is what Mesa writes when depth testing is off
    ; (v3dx_emit.c:346-348, PIPE_FUNC_ALWAYS, and the XML's Compare
    ; Function enum gives ALWAYS = 7).
    V3dClCfgBits(V3dCfgBitsWord(1, 1, 0, 7))

    V3dClPointSize(#TRI_F_ONE)
    V3dClLineWidth(#TRI_F_ONE)

    ; Half-width and half-height IN 1/256ths OF A PIXEL, as floats.
    ; 32 pixels * 256 = 8192.
    V3dClClipperXyScaling(#TRI_F_8192, #TRI_F_8192)
    ; Zs = Zc * 1 + 0, so the vertex shader's Zs is Zc unchanged.
    V3dClClipperZScaleOffset(#TRI_F_ONE, #TRI_F_ZERO)
    ; And the clip planes Mesa derives from the same two numbers:
    ; translate - scale and translate + scale, so -1 and +1.
    V3dClClipperZMinMax($BF800000, #TRI_F_ONE)
    ; The viewport centre, u14.8: 32 pixels is 8192.
    V3dClViewportOffset((#TRI_CX * 256), 0, (#TRI_CY * 256), 0)

    ; Zero because the fragment shader has no varyings at all.
    V3dClColorWriteMasks(0)
    V3dClZeroAllFlatShadeFlags()
    V3dClZeroAllNonperspFlags()
    V3dClZeroAllCentroidFlags()

    V3dClOcclusionQueryCounter(0)
    ; Coverage 1.0 as an f187 - the top sixteen bits of the f32 - and
    ; the four-sample mask Mesa writes for a non-MSAA surface.
    V3dClSampleState($3F80, $F)

    ; Vc = vcm_cache_size for both phases, and with no geometry shader
    ; that is the same number twice (Mesa mesa-24.3.4 src/broadcom/compiler/vir.c
    ; :2508-2515). Four is what :861-876's arithmetic gives for any
    ; VPM this part reports.
    V3dClVcmCacheSize(4, 4)
    V3dClGlShaderState(V3dShaderRecordAddr(), 8)

    V3dClVertexArrayPrims(#V3D_PRIM_TRIANGLES, 3, 0)

    r = V3dBclFinish()
  EndIf
  PutS("6   the bin list: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BCL")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("bin list bytes", V3dBclBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dBclStartAddr(), V3dBclBytes())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  7. THE RENDER LIST AND ITS GENERIC TILE LIST. Unchanged from the
  ;     clear: the render side of a draw and of a clear are the same
  ;     list, which is worth knowing and is why this stage did not
  ;     have to touch V3dRclBuild().
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRclBuild(#TRI_TILELIST, #TRI_TL_BYTES, #TRI_RCL, #TRI_RCL_BYTES)
  PutS("7   the render list: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RCL")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  RowDec("generic tile list bytes", V3dTileListBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dTileListStartAddr(), V3dTileListBytes())
  RowDec("render list bytes", V3dRclBytes())
  DumpBytes(V3dRclStartAddr(), V3dRclBytes())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  8. CACHE MAINTENANCE FOR THE FOUR BUFFERS V3dBinSubmit() DOES NOT
  ;     KNOW ABOUT.
  ;
  ;     V3dBinSubmit() cleans the bin list, the tile allocation pool
  ;     and the tile state, because those are the three it is handed.
  ;     The shader record, the vertex data, the uniform streams and
  ;     the QPU programs are reached through the record and the
  ;     library never sees their extents. WITH THE ARM MMU OFF THIS
  ;     COSTS NOTHING AND DOES NOTHING - every access is
  ;     Device-nGnRnE - and it is here anyway because the first
  ;     cacheable-DRAM run should not have to discover it.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  V3dCacheRange(#TRI_SHREC, V3dShaderRecordBytes())
  V3dCacheRange(#TRI_VERTS, 512)
  V3dCacheRange(#TRI_UNIF_CS, 256)
  V3dCacheRange(#TRI_CODE_CS, #TRI_CODE_SLOT * 3)
  V3dBarrier()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  9. THE BIN JOB. This one bins a real primitive.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dBinSubmit()
  PutS("8   bin submit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BINSUBMIT")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dBinWait(#TRI_WAIT_US)
  PutS("    bin wait: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("CLE_BFC before", V3dBinBfcBefore())
  RowHex("CLE_BFC after", V3dBinBfcAfter())
  RowHex("CLE_CT0CA", V3dBinCt0ca())
  RowHex("CLE_CT0EA", V3dBinCt0ea())
  RowHex("PTB_BPCA", V3dBinBpca())
  RowHex("PTB_BPCS", V3dBinBpcs())
  RowHex("CTL_INT_STS", V3dBinIntSts())
  RowHex("ERR_STAT", V3dBinErrStat())
  RowHex("MMU_CTL", V3dBinMmuCtl())
  RowHex("MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dBinVioAddr())
  RowDec("bin spins", V3dBinSpins())
  RowDec("OOM events", V3dBinOomCount())
  PutS("    the tile allocation pool, first 16 words:")
  PutNl()
  DumpBytes(#TRI_TALLOC, 64)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: BIN")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  10. THE RENDER JOB.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  r = V3dRenderSubmit()
  PutS("9   render submit: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  If r <> #V3D_OK
    PutS("verdict: RENDERSUBMIT")
    PutNl()
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  r = V3dRenderWait(#TRI_WAIT_US)
  PutS("    render wait: ")
  PutErr(r)
  PutNl()
  RowHex("CLE_RFC before", V3dRenderRfcBefore())
  RowHex("CLE_RFC after", V3dRenderRfcAfter())
  RowHex("CLE_CT1CA", V3dRenderCt1ca())
  RowHex("CLE_CT1EA", V3dRenderCt1ea())
  RowHex("CTL_INT_STS", V3dRenderIntSts())
  RowHex("ERR_STAT", V3dRenderErrStat())
  RowHex("MMU_CTL", V3dRenderMmuCtl())
  RowHex("MMU_VIO_ADDR", V3dRenderVioAddr())
  RowDec("render spins", V3dRenderSpins())
  RowDec("cache clean result", V3dRenderCleanResult())
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  11. THE PIXELS. This is the whole test.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Verify()
  VerifyGuard()

  PutS("10  the pixels")
  PutNl()
  RowDec("pixels total", #TRI_PIXELS)
  RowHex("triangle colour", #TRI_COLOR)
  RowDec("pixels triangle colour", nTri)
  RowHex("clear colour", #TRI_CLEAR)
  RowDec("pixels clear colour", nClear)
  RowDec("pixels still poison", nPoison)
  RowDec("pixels some other value", nOther)
  RowDec("first other, pixel index", firstOther)
  RowHex("first other, value", firstOtherVal)
  RowDec("bounding box min x", minX)
  RowDec("bounding box max x", maxX)
  RowDec("bounding box min y", minY)
  RowDec("bounding box max y", maxY)
  RowDec("guard words touched", guardTouched)
  PutNl()

  PutS("    the shape, both Y conventions, margin 2 px:")
  PutNl()
  RowDec("dir0 interior pixels", insideN0)
  RowDec("dir0 interior WRONG", insideBad0)
  RowDec("dir0 exterior pixels", outsideN0)
  RowDec("dir0 exterior WRONG", outsideBad0)
  RowDec("dir1 interior pixels", insideN1)
  RowDec("dir1 interior WRONG", insideBad1)
  RowDec("dir1 exterior pixels", outsideN1)
  RowDec("dir1 exterior WRONG", outsideBad1)
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  THE VERDICT.
  ;
  ;  A pass needs ALL of: no poison left anywhere, nothing outside the
  ;  two colours, the guard page untouched, and ONE of the two Y
  ;  conventions clean on both its interior and its exterior. The
  ;  interior count also has to be non-zero, or "nothing was drawn and
  ;  every exterior pixel is the clear colour" would pass.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ok = 0
  If insideN0 > 0
    If insideBad0 = 0
      If outsideBad0 = 0
        ok = 1
      EndIf
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If insideN1 > 0
    If insideBad1 = 0
      If outsideBad1 = 0
        ok = 2
      EndIf
    EndIf
  EndIf
  If nPoison <> 0 Or nOther <> 0 Or guardTouched <> 0
    ok = 0
  EndIf

  Select ok
    Case 1
      PutS("verdict: OK - triangle, Y increases with the stored row")
    Case 2
      PutS("verdict: OK - triangle, Y is flipped against the stored row")
    Default
      PutS("verdict: NO TRIANGLE")
  EndSelect
  PutNl()

  ProcedureReturn nTri
EndProcedure
